{"title":"1993 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pat Peano has a collection of numbers to label the pages of his scrapbook. He has an infinite number of 0's, 1's, 3's, 4's, 5's, 6's, 7's, 8's and 9's, but only twenty-two 2's.  How far can he number the pages of his scrapbook with these digits?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da325f583676c38e12d433f60c8d8f881c8182ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 22 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 99 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 112 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 119 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 199$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"402\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> two in the one-digit numbers.\n</p><p>The number of two-digit numbers with a two in the tens place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the number with a two in the ones place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus the digit two is used <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/40624ae61cda9f61df1c1b860675122d0f525c0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+9=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> times for the two digit numbers.\n</p><p>Now, Pat Peano only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf559d73fb34cf6ac7086922a2981c5b5e6fba1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22-1-19=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" /> remaining twos. You must subtract 1 because 22 is counted twice. The last numbers with a two that he can write are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419924dabadec1cbc40ad235df6230a545e2161f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$102$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3907e89ce5b06f13d78589b5d92624a8b41a7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$112$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. He can continue numbering the last couple pages without a two until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, with the last number he writes being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/6/d5638be9baf8f5052ad362dea28c8bd9e747fb71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}\\ 119}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"70\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; widt